On Feb 12, 7:47 pm, Daniel Lee <bear...@alum.mit.edu> wrote:
> Are you able to try with g++ 4.6? I think there's some part of the
> C++11 standard that isn't implemented in 4.4 that we use.
>
> If that works, microwaves must have g++ 4.6 in order to use Stan.

I can't install g++ 4.6 on that machine, but I can install 4.4.x and
4.5.x on my laptop, both of which fail to build that test.

That said, requiring 4.6 because of one build failure seems premature.
It's not as if the test builds but yields a wrong answer. If defining
that typedef is absolutely impossible with older versions of g++, then
I would be more in favor of ifdefing out the test.

To require 4.6 is basically to say that Stan can't run on the current
generation of stable Linux servers. Hotfoot, for example, defaults to g
++ 4.1.x (although it does have 4.4.x available, but nothing more
recent).

Ben

