Ben, it looks like the test does not compile. Did I misread it or is
it compiling and yielding incorrect answers?

Both are disturbing, the second is worse. (The first can be "fixed" by
using a more recent version of g++, the second points to a bug in the
compiler.) We've already had to deal with massive pain with
limitations of the different version of the compiler.

I'm not sure it is reasonable for Stan to be pre-C++11 compliant. I'll
have to think about it.

