You'll have to take that one up with andrew.  I only know
R2WinBugs and R2jags and Rcpp, but Andrew thought having the
R was tacky.

> If you ever intend to have them packaged
> for Linux distributions, having two source packages with the same name
> will cause some headaches. Finally, since stan the library is BSD and
> stan the R package is GPL, I'd say that having distinct names would be
> less legally confusing.

(R)?2(S|s)tan the R package will be BSD-ed, too.
Only the *combination* of R2stan and R become
GPL-ed.  That'll let us host on Google Code (which
doesn't or at least didn't allow GPL code hosting),
and also let people distribute all of (R)stan without
worrying about the GPL (unless they link to R and
redistribute).

